<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28747" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕphītis</span></b> , is,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a noxious, pestilential exhalation from the ground,
			mephitis</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saevamque exhalat opaca mephitim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulphureae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					3, 99</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Personified: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕphītis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕfi-tis</span></b> ),
			is, f., <i>a goddess who
				averts pestilential exhalations</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3,
			34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 93, 95, § 208</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1795</span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 7, 84</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lucus Mephitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, 7, § 49</span></i>
			 Müll.: aedes, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. 351,
			3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
